Ok, here's one for all you Happy NetHackers.
Try not to flame me too harshly.
<spoiler alert>




























As it now stands, unholy water is good for chaotics, and bad for lawfuls.
However, it still curses items for all alignments.
Is this just because the chaotic gods are perverse?  Shouldn't they reward
followers?  Holy water cures things for lawfuls, but unholy does nothing for
chaotics.  Unholy water should have _some_ beneficial effect on my barbarian.

Ok, now how about this?  I propose that items have alignments, like characters.
A blessed item would be the item that is the same alignment as the character.
This would reverse the polarity of chaotics, but if blessed and cursed items
occur with relatively the same frequency, so that lawful and chaotic items are
approximately balanced, there should be no problem.  

The problem with this system, however, is with the neutrals. Of course, you 
figured this out already.  So, how should they be dealt with?  Should chaotic
items be cursed and lawful items uncursed?  This seems to make sense, but it
interrupts the orderly progression cursed-uncursed-blessed.

Well, there it is, have fun with it.  Post suggestions or additions (or praises :)
so that we can all see them.  Flame in email, don't waste the bandwidth.

